Z||000000||Phantom Rage||02-13-2000||10:16 AM||||Sorry if this was already covered, but there are a whole lot of post out there.  I have to replace my clutch slave cyl for my 88-5 speed(Isuzu). When I first bougt my car I had to repace my clutch, slave, master; Pep Boys did the install.  Two years later I have to replace the master and slave again.  The problem is that when I asked the parts guy for a new slave, he gave me one that looked different form the one they put on 2 years ago.  I told him there must be a mistake but he reconfirmed that it was correct, so I dedided to call a few other Pep Boys to see if that was indeed the right slave cyl,they also said that it was the correct one.  Apperently the guys at Pep Boys put on one for a 4 speed, according to there parts book.  I not sure if they are right though.  I bought both for the time being, the one that is on my car right now is longer(about 1 inch)and is thinner, also it does not have a boot to cover the rod, just a rubber cover over the rod entry point, the other has a boot to cover the hole rod except for the end of it. The 88 5-speed one(according to them) lookes just like the one I had to replace on my brothers 88 formula.  Can I use either one.  Is the slave on the 5 speed getrag the same as my 5 speed Isuzu or does the Isuzu share the same as the 4 speed Isuzu.  I'm not sure if I trust their parts database, since they put the four speed one on 2 years back and now gave me one that is supposed to be the correct one, yet is different.  Ahhhhh Please help!!!! Thx<p>[This message has been edited by Phantom Rage (edited 02-13-2000).]||||reg||9
